      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for safe-record defensive guards",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`isRecordWithoutThrowing`, `readRecordValue`, `copyArrayEntries`, and `copyRecordEntries` are exported defensive guards against hostile objects with 0% test coverage.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx --input-type=module -e \"\nimport { readRecordValue, copyArrayEntries, copyRecordEntries } from './src/shared/safe-record.ts';\n\n// readRecordValue: Proxy with throwing get trap → returns undefined\nconst hostGet = new Proxy({name:'test'}, { get() { throw new Error('boom'); } });\nconsole.log('throwing get:', JSON.stringify(readRecordValue(hostGet, 'name')));\n\n// copyArrayEntries: array-like with throwing length getter → returns []\nconst badArr = Object.defineProperty({0:'a',1:'b'}, 'length', { get() { throw new Error('boom'); } });\nconsole.log('throwing length:', JSON.stringify(copyArrayEntries(badArr)));\n\n// copyRecordEntries: Proxy with throwing ownKeys trap → returns []\nconst hostKeys = new Proxy({a:1,b:2}, { ownKeys() { throw new Error('boom'); } });\nconsole.log('throwing ownKeys:', JSON.stringify(copyRecordEntries(hostKeys)));\n\"\n\nthrowing get: undefined\nthrowing length: []\nthrowing ownKeys: []\n\nAll three guarded helpers return safe defaults on hostile input.\n\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/safe-record.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  15 passed (15)\n```\n",
